    THE READING, and its limits are stated because they are real. The two arms
    disagree 65 against 1 over the same 65 members. The captured distribution --
    64 with an action, 1 without -- is what a grammar registry should look like;
    65 rules with no action is not. So the bare arm is the suspect one.

    ⚠ THE CONTROL IS WHAT MAKES THIS A MECHANISM AND NOT JUST A DISAGREEMENT,
    AND IT RULES OUT THE OBVIOUS STORY. `== 999` reads 0, not 65, so the bare
    comparison is NOT blanket-truthy -- it does discriminate on the constant.
    Both readings together fit one account: the bare name resolves to a node
