    That is consistent with it reaching the GroupField DEFINITION (incant/setup
    registers actionTypE=406) rather than the cursor's property. CONSISTENT
    WITH, not diagnosed -- per the standing split, reproduction proves the
    symptom and never the cause.

    ⚠ AND THE LAST-MENTIONED STORY IS KILLED BY THE LAST ROW. The obvious rival
    account was that the bare read simply had no cursor in scope, since the
    statement before it is `++atTotal;` on a local. So the bare test is asked a
    SECOND time, after `atCur` has been mentioned by name. It still reads 65.
    The position inside the body does not move it.

    ⚠⚠ THE REMEDY HAS A SPELLING, AND THE NATURAL ONE CAPTURES NOTHING. The
    captured arm was first written `atLocal = atCur.actionTypE;` -- ordinary
    assignment, the obvious way to capture-then-test -- and it read 0 zeros and
    65 non-zeros, agreeing with nothing and measuring nothing. `:=` reads 1 and
