    ⚠ WHAT IS NOT CLAIMED. This does not convict parser:47, f31:77 or any other
    corpus site: those walk a rule's own children while this walks a registry's
    members, and no fixture here has run against their populations. It says the
    SHAPE disagrees with itself and names which arm looks wrong. The verdict is
    Tony's.

    ⚠ ANTI-VACUITY, TWO ROWS AND BOTH ARE LOAD-BEARING. The population must be
    non-zero -- two arms that both walk nothing agree perfectly and assert
    nothing. AND the captured non-zero count must be above zero: if every member
    read actionTypE == 0, an always-truthy bare arm and a correct captured arm
    would produce the SAME number and the fixture could not tell them apart. A
    zero-expecting row needs a non-zero sibling, and that is it.

    ⚠ AN EARLIER DRAFT MEASURED NOTHING AND SAID SO LOUDLY, which is the only
